I. Ensure XMing is runnin with access control disabled
- open powershel and launch XMing with the -ac flag:
      "Start-Process "C:\Program Files (x86)\Xming\Xming.exe" -ArgumentList "-ac"

II. Grant MariaDB remote access in HeidiSQL
- Open HeidiSQL, connect to your local database, open a Query tab, and run:
    "GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON svg_travel_db.* TO 'root'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY 'Test12';
    FLUSH PRIVILEGES;"

III. Build and load the Docker image into Minikube
- Run the following in PowerShell:
    "# 1. Build the Docker image locally
        docker build -t amirdirin/svg_3012_db_k8s:latest .

    "# 2. Save and load image tarball into Minikube
        docker save amirdirin/svg_3012_db_k8s:latest -o app-image.tar
        minikube image load app-image.tar
        Remove-Item app-image.tar "

IV. Apply Kubernetes manifests and start the pod
- Deploy the updated configuration and trigger a restart:
    "kubectl apply -f k8s-manifests.yaml
     kubectl rollout restart deployment javafx-travel-app"

V. Monitor application logs
- Stream the logs to confirm connection and verify the GUI window renders on your desktop:
    "kubectl logs -l app=javafx-travel-app -f"